{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>For. From of old.</b> And if it has a shureq, it is like a participle [חולם], and the sense of אתמול is from aforetime." "<b>Its Topheth.</b> The name of a place defiled around Jerusalem, and there they will cast all refuse and smoke will rise from it, and the sense is that HaShem prepared it for the camp of Assyria." "<b>It too is prepared for the king.</b> The sense is that every prince and officer will be destroyed, and some say that it is an allusion to the king of Assyria." "<b>Its pyre.</b> From the root of מדורה (Ezekiel 24:9): the place of the fire's burning." "<b>The breath of YHWH.</b> That comes swiftly, and this is by way of allegory concerning the decrees that come in haste."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra's text reads היא (feminine); the correction הוא (masculine) is noted in the marginal variant צ״ל הוא, likely to agree with the masculine referent."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:13.116568720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}